        "text": "You've probably also heard about blockchain's use cases in the decentralized finance space. The idea of DEFI is to create a more open, inclusive, decentralized and transparent financial system that runs on top of public blockchain systems. By removing financial intermediaries, DEFI gives people direct control of their assets and permits them to conduct peer to peer transactions. Moreover, blockchain technology is quite reliable in storing records with high data integrity, while enabling many different participants to use the same database as a shared source of truth. Supply chains involve many different companies that have to integrate their systems with each other to handle goods. From suppliers to consumers, often across borders and through customs. Blockchain technology can make interactions between businesses smoother and more efficient, which ultimately benefits the economy and the consumer.",
